Instructions to run the project:

1. accept the project
2. click on "back to project"
3. click on API keys
4. click on "Create new secret keys"
5. copy the key
6. in the server folder, create a file named ".env", note it may have disappeared due to it being ignored for security reasons, try "nano .env", and write "OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR_OWN_KEY". no space in between, replace YOUR_OWN_KEY with your API key
7. run "npm install cors" in server folder, it is not nesscary but we are saving it for security
8. when running the web, first cd to server, and then run "node index.js" in your terminal, you should see something similar to "Server running at http://localhost:3000"
9. go to the extension page, turn it on, click the label, open the website and upload the pdf that is inside the project folder called test example

Some notes:
1. use the example files in test example folder first, the code still has some issues with longer essays
2. it is ok if the processing takes time for now
3. always f12 for console outputs
4. Don't put it in the second window slot. I don't know why, but just don't, haha(for fun)

Common Debug:
1. my extension says it cannot open my pdf
	- run "node index.js" in the server folder before you use the extension

1.1 my terminal says it cannot find cors package
	- run "npm install cors"

2. my extension does not align links/long pdf cleanly
	- we are still developing

3. my picture looks blurry
	- it is because it was blurry in the original file
